//   → [quitchars dismisses the More] → getpos(&cc, TRUE, "the desired destination")
//   → handle_tip(TIP_GETPOS) → farlook tip window (NHW_TEXT)
//   → [quitchars dismisses the tip] → pline("(For instructions type a '?')")
//                                   → pline("Move cursor to %s:", goal)
//   → getpos cursor loop → dotravel_target()
//
// getpos prompt (C ref: getpos.c:845,861):
//   pline #1: "(For instructions type a '?')" → redotoplin
//   pline #2: "Move cursor to the desired destination:" → addtopl
//   Combined topline: "(For instructions type a '?')  Move cursor to the desired destination:"
//   cursor at the getpos cursor's screen position (cx-1, cy+1), which starts at
//   the hero (getpos.c:848 cx = ccp->x) when iflags.travelcc is unset.
//
// THE CURSOR LOOP IS NOW THE REAL getpos() (this file, C getpos.c:771-1170) —
// the same body dojump() and scrolltele() already call.  It used to be a single
// unconditional nhgetch() here, with the tip window and the two prompt plines
// the recorded travel presses '>' at the cursor prompt, C runs the symbol search
